# id: M47-superseded-split-applied-anyway
# covering-test: TestASupersededSplitIsRefused
# package: ./store/
# expect: killed
# power: n/a -- the sweep cannot produce this schedule. Raft's figure-8 rule serialises it: a new leader must commit an entry of its own before it can commit the previous term's split, and committing it means applying it, which moves the extent before a second split can be proposed from it. Zero firings in 300 A4 seeds, recorded in DESIGN-A4 section 10 as an unexercised path rather than as evidence. The guard is induced directly instead, which is what a floor could not have told us
# mutates: the extent guard requires ALL THREE mismatches instead of any one, so a split superseded by an earlier one is applied anyway. A split superseded by an earlier one then moves the left range's End BACKWARDS past the first cut and mints a range overlapping the one already there, so two ranges claim the same keys and their replicas disagree about which entry is at index one of a range born twice
